from mkchar import mk
mk("Noriko_Asano.md","Noriko Asano","2","Book 5","Book 12","Books 5, 12 (chapter files)","Yumi_Asano.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md, Jota_Withers.md",
"The strongest member of the old Asano clan and its patriarch's mother, who takes control from her son and opposes Jason's family; she is matriarch of the old clan by Book 12.",
["Introduced as \"the strongest member of the Asano clan and the patriarch's mother\", presiding with eight elders at a low table (Book 5, Ch36 L3).",
 "She argues the clan must seize the chance only it has, that there is only shame in weakness and that \"only the strongest shall rise\" (Book 5, Ch36 L11-16), and tells the others not to inform Mei and Akari, so they act as a mask for the clan's own plans (Book 5, Ch36 L32).",
 "She is contemptuous of honour (\"You sound like your new white friend, Asano\", Book 5, Ch36 L89) and Jason rejects any connection: \"My Asano family and your Asano clan henceforth have no connections, Noriko\" (Book 5, Ch37 L92).",
 "She wrests control of the clan from her son, the former head Shiro, whose closest family settle in Asano Village (Book 5, Ch52 L68).",
 "In Book 12 she is matriarch of the Asano clan hosting Jota Withers, makes daily visits and supplies servants (Book 12, Ch63 L19); she explains the government seized land from the \"upstart clan\" and gave it to the \"true Asano clan\" (Book 12, Ch63 L30)."],
"Stern, brusque and proud; she measures people by strength and treats compromise as weakness.",
timeline=["Book 5: seizes the clan and confronts Jason (Book 5, Ch36-37, Ch52).","Book 12: hosts the pirate admiral Jota Withers (Book 12, Ch63)."])
mk("Li_Li_Mei.md","Li Li Mei","2","Book 4","Book 13","Books 4-6, 12, 13 (chapter files)","Jason_Asano.md, ../06_Places/Minor_Places/Boko.md",
"A Chinese silver-ranker and daughter of Li Ning who deals with Jason on Earth in Books 4-6, ends up in Pallimustus, is found hiding in Boko, and becomes a political figure in Book 13.",
["Silver-rank daughter of Li Ning, meeting Jason in a business resort lobby; she hopes for a \"more modest collaboration in the future\" (Book 4, Ch63 L25-28).",
 "She appears beside the dome and portal with two Chinese gold-rankers (Book 6, Ch5 L59; Book 6, Ch6 L16-21).",
 "In Book 12 she has lived in Boko for years (Book 12, Ch30 L71-74); Jason finds her there, more than fifteen years after they last met (Book 12, Ch30 L80; Book 12, Ch31 L3-12). She stays near him during Boko's destruction (Book 12, Ch32 L18) and its aftermath (Book 12, Ch37).",
 "Jason uses her as a test subject for refining his control of the System (Book 12, Ch48 L26) and counts her among the Earthlings who roamed (Book 12, Ch48 L33).",
 "By Book 13 she is one of the few with political experience in both worlds (Book 13, Ch1015 L40), meeting the international committee or the Chinese delegation, joined by her gold-rank uncle Li Chen (Book 13, Ch960 L16)."],
"Controlled and watchful; she hides her expressions and adapts quickly to a new world's rules.",
timeline=["Book 4: negotiates at Castle Reach (Book 4, Ch63).","Book 6: arrives with the Chinese gold-rankers (Book 6, Ch5-6).","Book 12: found in Boko; helps through its destruction (Book 12, Ch30-37).","Book 13: negotiator for the handoff (Book 13, Ch960, Ch1015)."])
mk("Ketevan_Arziani.md","Ketevan Arziani","2","Book 4","Book 12","Books 4, 5, 11, 12 (chapter files)","Anna_Tilden.md, Yumi_Asano.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
"An analytical Network officer in Sydney, Anna Tilden's assistant, who later becomes Yumi Asano's chief of staff.",
["Anna places a lot of trust in her analytical abilities (Book 4, Ch5 L10); she investigates a hospital event up the coast (Book 4, Ch8 L83).",
 "Her formal title is Assistant to the Director of Operations, Sydney branch; Jason guesses she is about thirty, athletic, with short brown hair (Book 4, Ch46 L82).",
 "Jason saves her life with one of Shade's bodies forming a parachute (Book 4, Ch47 L28; Book 4, Ch59 L13).",
 "She leads the Network defectors' intake and sits on calls with the Sydney branch (Book 5, Ch9 L67; Book 5, Ch36 L33).",
 "After the Network's Australian branch breaks up, Yumi hires her for her administrative skill; in Book 11 she doubts Jason's plans while Yumi has faith (Book 11, Ch36 L54-64).",
 "In Book 12 she is chief of staff to the clan matriarch (Book 12, Ch40 L52) and drives Anna through Saint-Étienne (Book 12, Ch41 L3-14)."],
"Brisk and sceptical, with an analyst's habit of testing leaps of logic.")
mk("Miles_Cotezee.md","Miles Cotezee","1","Book 6","Book 12","Books 6, 7, 12 (chapter files)","Humphrey_Geller.md, ../05_Organisations/Adventure_Society.md, ../06_Places/Vitesse.md",
"A senior Vitesse Adventure Society administrator whose silver rank comes entirely from cores and who supervises missions in the surge.",
["A senior administrator, silver rank \"entirely from cores\", with a paper, knowledge, rune and scribe essence combination (Book 6, Ch47 L878).",
 "He briefs Humphrey's team in his office (Book 7, Ch12 L69) and prepares a strike force against the Purity stronghold with marshalling instructions (Book 7, Ch16 L3, L75).",
 "He supervises a Book 7 mission with the temporary team leader Kenneth (Book 7, Ch25 L4) and meets Jason's team at the outworlder arrival (Book 7, Ch36 L65).",
 "In Book 12 he hurries across the Vitesse campus of the Magic Research Association after Jason's return and shares tea with Clive's assistant (Book 12, Ch1 L53; Book 12, Ch2 L50)."],
"A harried, courteous official who runs paperwork and logistics.")
